\subsection{Massive Multimodal Embedding Benchmark}

The MMEB is a benchmark designed to evaluate the performance of multimodal embedding models on a wide range of tasks. It consists of 36 datasets that cover four meta-tasks: classification, visual question answering, multimodal retrieval, and visual grounding. The benchmark is designed to be comprehensive and challenging, and it provides a fair and objective way to compare the performance of different models. The MMEB is an important tool for researchers and practitioners who are interested in developing and evaluating multimodal embedding models. By using the MMEB, they can ensure that their models are performing well on a wide range of tasks, and they can identify areas for improvement. The MMEB is also useful for comparing different models and for selecting the best model for a particular application. Overall, the MMEB is a valuable resource for anyone who is working on multimodal embedding models, and it will continue to be an important benchmark for years to come.

